{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"docsStarts":1},{"foundation":2,"assurance":3},"/foundation/docs/","/assurance/docs/getting-started/"],"uses":{}},null,{"type":"data","data":[{"docs":1,"source":44},{"nav":2,"slugs":43,"first":6},[3,7,11,15,19,23,27,31,35,39],{"name":4,"href":5,"slug":6},"Getting started","/assurance/docs/getting-started/","getting-started",{"name":8,"href":9,"slug":10},"Scenarios","/assurance/docs/scenarios/","scenarios",{"name":12,"href":13,"slug":14},"Business context","/assurance/docs/business-context/","business-context",{"name":16,"href":17,"slug":18},"Evidence","/assurance/docs/evidence/","evidence",{"name":20,"href":21,"slug":22},"The CLI","/assurance/docs/cli/","cli",{"name":24,"href":25,"slug":26},"Running in CI","/assurance/docs/ci/","ci",{"name":28,"href":29,"slug":30},"Adapters","/assurance/docs/adapters/","adapters",{"name":32,"href":33,"slug":34},"Analyzers","/assurance/docs/analyzers/","analyzers",{"name":36,"href":37,"slug":38},"Privacy","/assurance/docs/privacy/","privacy",{"name":40,"href":41,"slug":42},"Performance","/assurance/docs/performance/","performance",[6,10,14,18,22,26,30,34,38,42],{"repo":45,"version":46},"https://github.com/AHRConsulting/Ahr.Assurance","0.1.0"],"uses":{"params":["product"]}},{"type":"data","data":[{"slug":1,"page":2},"analyzers",{"slug":1,"title":3,"html":4,"headings":5,"source":28},"Analyzers","\u003Cp>The analyzers come with every adapter. They report mistakes that compile but make a test pass, fail or break silently.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"table-wrap\">\u003Ctable>\n\u003Cthead>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Cth>ID\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Severity\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Reports\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Code fix\u003C/th>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/thead>\n\u003Ctbody>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"#ahra101\">AHRA101\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Warning\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>A step lambda returns the task it assigns\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Use a block body\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"#ahra102\">AHRA102\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Warning\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>A scenario is not verified\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Await \u003Ccode>VerifyAsync()\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"#ahra103\">AHRA103\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Warning\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>A resource is disposed before the scenario runs\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Make the method async and await\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"#ahra105\">AHRA105\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Warning\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>A scenario's steps are out of order or incomplete\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>—\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"#ahra106\">AHRA106\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Warning\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Scenarios share a name and have no ID\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>—\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"#ahra107\">AHRA107\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Warning\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>An inline scenario is stored for reuse\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>—\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"#ahra108\">AHRA108\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Info\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>A step property can be static\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Make the step static\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/tbody>\n\u003C/table>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>Change a rule's severity in \u003Ccode>.editorconfig\u003C/code>, for example \u003Ccode>dotnet_diagnostic.AHRA106.severity = none\u003C/code>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"ahra101\">AHRA101\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>A step lambda returns the task it assigns,\u003C/strong> so the step waits for it.\u003C/p>\n\u003C!-- diagnostic -->\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Given\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"Work starts\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, () \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> pending \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> StartAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">())      \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// waits for StartAsync\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Given\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"Work starts\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, () \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> { pending \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> StartAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(); })  \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// stores the task\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"ahra102\">AHRA102\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>A scenario is not verified.\u003C/strong> A scenario does nothing until \u003Ccode>VerifyAsync()\u003C/code> runs it, so the test passes without checking anything. Await or return its task.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"ahra103\">AHRA103\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>A resource is disposed before the scenario runs.\u003C/strong> In a method that isn't \u003Ccode>async\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>using\u003C/code> disposes the resource when the method returns, before the scenario runs.\u003C/p>\n\u003C!-- diagnostic -->\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">public\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\"> Task\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> Cancels\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">()\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">    using\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> var\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> cancellation \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> new\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\"> CancellationTokenSource\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">();\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">    return\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Scenario.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Define\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">..\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">.).\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">When\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"It is cancelled\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">, () \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> cancellation.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Cancel\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">())\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">..\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">VerifyAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">();   \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// disposed too early\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>The fix makes the method \u003Ccode>async\u003C/code> and awaits \u003Ccode>VerifyAsync()\u003C/code>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"ahra105\">AHRA105\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>A scenario's steps are out of order or incomplete.\u003C/strong> Steps go \u003Ccode>Given\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>When\u003C/code>, then \u003Ccode>Then\u003C/code>. \u003Ccode>And\u003C/code> can't start a scenario, a scenario needs a \u003Ccode>When\u003C/code>, and its last step is a \u003Ccode>Then\u003C/code> or a throws step. A \u003Ccode>When\u003C/code> after a \u003Ccode>Then\u003C/code> starts another action.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"ahra106\">AHRA106\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Scenarios share a name and have no ID,\u003C/strong> so they are reported as one. Give each a distinct name or an \u003Ccode>id\u003C/code>. Parameterised tests aren't reported, because each row has its own ID.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"ahra107\">AHRA107\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>An inline scenario is stored for reuse.\u003C/strong> An inline scenario runs once, with its test's local state. Define it inside each test, or use a typed scenario with a context factory.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"ahra108\">AHRA108\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>A step property can be static.\u003C/strong> The fix makes it static and updates its uses.\u003C/p>\n",[6,10,13,16,19,22,25],{"id":7,"text":8,"level":9},"ahra101","AHRA101",2,{"id":11,"text":12,"level":9},"ahra102","AHRA102",{"id":14,"text":15,"level":9},"ahra103","AHRA103",{"id":17,"text":18,"level":9},"ahra105","AHRA105",{"id":20,"text":21,"level":9},"ahra106","AHRA106",{"id":23,"text":24,"level":9},"ahra107","AHRA107",{"id":26,"text":27,"level":9},"ahra108","AHRA108","docs/analyzers.md"],"uses":{"params":["page","product"]}}]}
